":142},{\"_109\":110,\"_111\":112,\"_113\":114},\"kind\",\"callout\",\"variant\",\"transparent\",\"children\",[115,116,117],{\"_109\":135,\"_136\":137,\"_138\":-7,\"_113\":139},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":124},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":119},\"p\",[120],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":122,\"_123\":-7},\"text\",\"For enterprise users, sharing can be turned off entirely from workspace settings.\",\"marks\",[125,126,127],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":134,\"_123\":-7},{\"_109\":129,\"_26\":130,\"_113\":131},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":128,\"_123\":-7},\".\",\"a\",\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference#tag/Projects\",[132],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":133,\"_123\":-7},\"Compliance API\",\"Project owners can remove members individually. Editors can add members, but not remove them. The Compliance API supports isolate project. Learn more about what’s supported in the \",\"h\",\"level\",2,\"anchorId\",[140],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":141,\"_123\":-7},\"How can I un-share a project?\",[143,144,145,146],{\"_109\":135,\"_136\":137,\"_138\":-7,\"_113\":162},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":153},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":150},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":147},[148],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":149,\"_123\":-7},\"Members can see a branched chat while it remains in the shared project. Whether the chat can be moved elsewhere depends on the project’s memory settings and available actions.\",[151],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":152,\"_123\":-7},\"Branching lets you explore a different direction or “remix” the thread without changing the original conversation—especially useful for testing alternate drafts, refining logic, or building on a teammate’s work.\",[154,155,156],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":161,\"_123\":-7},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":158,\"_123\":159},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":157,\"_123\":-7},\", not collaborated on synchronously.\",\"branched\",[160],\"b\",\"Chats in shared projects can be \",[163],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":164,\"_123\":-7},\"Can members work together on the same chat?\",[166,167,168],{\"_109\":135,\"_136\":137,\"_138\":-7,\"_113\":185},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":182},{\"_109\":169,\"_170\":171},\"ul\",\"items\",[172,173],[178],[174],{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":175},[176],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":177,\"_123\":-7},\"List Project Shared Users: See who is in a shared project\",{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":179},[180],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":181,\"_123\":-7},\"Isolate project: Removes all users except the owner\",[183],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":184,\"_123\":-7},\"The compliance API includes the following shared projects information:\",[186],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":187,\"_123\":-7},\"Is the compliance API supported for shared projects?\",[189,190],{\"_109\":135,\"_136\":137,\"_138\":-7,\"_113\":194},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":191},[192],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":193,\"_123\":-7},\"Yes, for messages in an existing project chat. If the first message uses a custom GPT, the conversation starts as a chat with that GPT and appears outside the project.\",[195],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":196,\"_123\":-7},\"Can I use a custom GPT in a project?\",[198,199,200,201,202],{\"_109\":135,\"_136\":137,\"_138\":-7,\"_113\":231},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":228},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":225},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":212},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":203},[204,205,206],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":211,\"_123\":-7},{\"_109\":129,\"_26\":207,\"_113\":208},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":128,\"_123\":-7},\"https://help.openai.com/articles/7925741\",[209],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":210,\"_123\":-7},\"Sharing conversations from ChatGPT\",\"For more information about shared links, see: \",[213,214,215,216,217],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":224,\"_123\":-7},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":222,\"_123\":223},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":221,\"_123\":-7},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":219,\"_123\":220},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":218,\"_123\":-7},\" until they join the project.\",\"access that chat\",[160],\" \",\"users will not be able to\",[160],\"Note that if you share a single chat from a shared project, \",[226],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":227,\"_123\":-7},\"A shared conversation link does not give recipients access to the rest of the project. For personal accounts, it includes the content available when the link was created or updated. Links from managed workspaces can include later messages, subject to workspace access and sharing settings.\",[229],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":230,\"_123\":-7},\"When you share a project, members can view its chats, files, and other members, and they can create or branch conversations. Members can move eligible chats into the project when Move to project is available.\",[232],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":233,\"_123\":-7},\"How does sharing a chat link differ from sharing a project?\",[235,236],{\"_109\":135,\"_136\":137,\"_138\":-7,\"_113\":240},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":237},[238],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":239,\"_123\":-7},\"Chat responses will only reference uploaded files and content shared directly in the project. If a member adds a file or context to a shared project, ChatGPT may use that information in responses visible to other members to make responses more relevant.\",[241],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":242,\"_123\":-7},\"Can ChatGPT’s responses in shared projects include private or internal data?\",[244,245],{\"_109\":135,\"_136\":137,\"_138\":-7,\"_113\":249},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":246},[247],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":248,\"_123\":-7},\"Yes. Workspace owners can enable or disable project sharing and use role-based permissions to decide who can share projects.\",[250],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":251,\"_123\":-7},\"Can workspace owners control access to shared projects?\",[253,254],{\"_109\":135,\"_136\":137,\"_138\":-7,\"_113\":258},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":255},[256],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":257,\"_123\":-7},\"All members of a project can view and download files added to the project.\",[259],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":260,\"_123\":-7},\"Can members download files from the shared project?\",[262,263,264,265],{\"_109\":135,\"_136\":137,\"_138\":-7,\"_113\":290},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":287},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":279},{\"_109\":266,\"_267\":268,\"_269\":270,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":274,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":278},\"img\",\"src\",\"https://images.ctfassets.net/j22is2dtoxu1/intercom-img-c90ba56d8bf5a4cd421a0284/367f7ade802e7a79e559d88c9be9fc96/d8280cce-0bd8-43c6-80ab-456becae05f0\",\"alt\",\"Image\",\"align\",\"center\",\"width\",490,\"height\",426,\"contentType\",\"image/png\",[280,281,282],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":286,\"_123\":-7},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":284,\"_123\":285},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":283,\"_123\":-7},\" to review its members.\",\"Share\",[160],\"The shared-project indicator appears only when a project uses the default icon. If you chose a different icon or color, open the project and select \",[288],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":289,\"_123\":-7},\"If you used the default icon when creating the project, sharing updates the sidebar icon to show that the project is shared.\",[291],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":292,\"_123\":-7},\"How can I tell if a project is shared?\",[294,295],{\"_109\":135,\"_136\":137,\"_138\":-7,\"_113\":303},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":296},[297,298,299],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":302,\"_123\":-7},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":284,\"_123\":301},{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":300,\"_123\":-7},\" to see members’ names, email addresses, and any invited groups. Each chat shows the profile icon of the person who created it.\",[160],\"Project members can view the project’s chats, files, and member list. Select \",[304],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":305,\"_123\":-7},\"What’s visible in a shared project?\",[307,308,309,310,311,312],{\"_109\":135,\"_136\":137,\"_138\":-7,\"_113\":374},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":371},{\"_109\":169,\"_170\":345},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":342},{\"_109\":169,\"_170\":316},{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":313},[314],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":315,\"_123\":-7},\"Example: Q4 planning hub (analyze quarterly data with your team)\",[317,318,319,320,321],[338],[334],[330],[326],[322],{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":323},[324],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\":325,\"_123\":-7},\"Best for team alignment, faster onboarding, and knowledge capture\",{\"_109\":118,\"_113\":327},[328],{\"_109\":121,\"_121\